    "body": "## Problem\nEditorConfig uses `[!seq]` for a negated character class (https://spec.editorconfig.org/#glob-expressions), but `glob2regpat()` keeps the `!` literal, so `[!a]` matches `a` or `!` and nothing else. For example, Checkmk's `.editorconfig` has a `[checks/[!.]*]` section, which Nvim applies only to dotfiles in `checks/`, the opposite of what it says.\n\n## Solution\nConvert `[!` to `[^` before calling `glob2regpat()`. Added a `\"[!seq]\" glob excludes seq` case to `test/functional/plugin/editorconfig_spec.lua`; it fails without the change and passes with it.\n\nAI-assisted: this change was written with an AI coding agent.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
